{"step_index":114,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:35:50Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-09T15:35:50Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-09T15:35:50Z\nFile Path: `file:///workspace/skill/references/setup.md`\nTotal Lines: 17\nTotal Bytes: 1991\nShowing lines 1 to 17\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Setup interview\n2: \n3: Inspect the request, available project instructions, existing workspaces, tools, and supplied evidence. Resolve facts through inspection. Ask one consequential question at a time, explain the trade-off, and recommend an answer when helpful. Reuse established answers, including a prior grill. Stop interviewing once shared understanding and necessary authority are concrete; do not make the owner preselect every future objective.\n4: \n5: Establish:\n6: \n7: - The product, broad responsibility, ongoing or bounded scope, and what worthwhile progress means. The agent can choose concrete objectives within it.\n8: - Relevant evidence, access, measurement definitions, observation needs, and how implementation and outcomes will be checked. Match the method to the domain.\n9: - Standing permission for the applicable actions, including deployment, rollback, and communication, with reserved owner decisions explicit.\n10: - Optional limits and any project cost instructions. Use the owner's own usage sources and shared allowance rules; named tools are examples, not required providers.\n11: - Related work, the product boundary for shared history, discovery of actual changes, and how interference is coordinated.\n12: - Initial timing, wait/pause/manual-resume/termination policy, routine reporting cadence and authorized destination, and immediate-notice arrangements.\n13: - A suitable existing scheduler, or the proposed scheduler setup when one is missing. Use [scheduling.md](scheduling.md) to inspect available tools and preserve the project's existing choice.\n14: - A readable file workspace that preserves the brief, actions, evidence, corrections, and pending work across fresh sessions.\n15: \n16: Save the agreed brief, unresolved prerequisites, and concrete initial continuation plan. Do not infer authorization from an empty answer, a fixed questionnaire, or the passage of time. Carry already-granted authority into the task's registration and subsequent runs. New facts can still require a later owner decision.\n17: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
