{"step_index":125,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:36:50Z","content":"I have completed the handoff review following `$long-horizon` and recorded the dated recommendation in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Recommendation\n\n- **Selected Onboarding Improvement:** **Mobile Status Filters for Small Workspaces** (addressing ticket [`record-e36f0fe1aa`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-0131162d69.md), submitted 2026-09-05).\n- **Why Not the Digest Request:** Ticket [`record-5f1a34c149`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-0131162d69.md) (submitted date unknown) reflects unmigrated legacy per-user daily preferences that override workspace settings for contributors subscribed before July 12 ([`record-f233630dab.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-f233630dab.md)). However, this feature originated in the retired `notification-reset` responsibility ([brief](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/notification-reset/brief.md)), which was terminated July 31. Under [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md), terminated responsibilities cannot be resumed under standing authority without an owner mandate.\n- **What Was Tried vs. What Actually Happened (Status Filters):**\n  - The handoff in [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md) assumed Focus Shelf was abandoned after low use. That was based on an erroneous metric ([`record-8a2203deaa.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-8a2203deaa.md)) that included bot accounts; human usage was actually 28% ([`record-661a77e48d.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-661a77e48d.md)).\n  - The real cause of the June 2 rollback ([`record-ecc0d14c71.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-ecc0d14c71.md)) was synchronous query latency on workspaces with >50k tasks. This was resolved on desktop on August 30 by introducing asynchronous count queries ([`record-b9a1361197.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md)), achieving 21% human desktop adoption ([`record-dfcc7fb912.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-dfcc7fb912.md)).\n  - The mobile component is already available in draft state ([`record-b9a1361197.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md)), but mobile was never exposed to users.\n- **Next Useful Action This Week:**\n  1. Inspect the draft mobile status filter component ([`record-b9a1361197.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md)) and verify primary filter support (\"waiting\").\n  2. Ensure the mobile implementation uses asynchronous count queries to prevent latency regressions.\n  3. Prepare a reversible mobile pilot targeted at small workspaces (≤100 tasks, matching `record-e36f0fe1aa`).\n  4. Flag the digest finding to Sam as an out-of-scope contributor preference migration issue requiring explicit owner direction.\n\nPlease review the full audit, evidence citations, and uncertainty analysis in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md)."}
